[10.24,"o","Implement a microservices architecture using a sharded message queue (e.g., Kafka) for task distribution. Use stateless agents with unique request IDs for idempotency and exponential backoff for retries. Apply cost controls via resource quotas and budgets. Enable observability through centralized logging and monitoring (e.g., Prometheus). Tradeoffs: increased complexity and maintenance overhead. Failure modes include queue overload and partial service outages, mitigated by dynamic scaling and circuit breakers.\r\n"]
